### Payment Gateway Sim: end-to-end demo
### Open in IntelliJ IDEA and run the requests top to bottom (HTTP Client).
### Values captured from responses are reused in later requests.

### 1. Onboard a merchant (the API key is only shown once)
POST http://localhost:8081/api/v1/merchants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Kedai Kopi Cyberjaya",
  "email": "owner@kedaikopi.example",
  "feeBps": 250
}

> {%
    client.global.set("merchantId", response.body.id);
    client.global.set("apiKey", response.body.apiKey);
%}

### 2. Tokenize a card (in real life the checkout page calls this, not the merchant server)
POST http://localhost:8083/api/v1/tokens
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "pan": "4242 4242 4242 4242",
  "expiryMonth": 12,
  "expiryYear": 2030,
  "cardholderName": "Ahmad Test"
}

> {% client.global.set("cardToken", response.body.token); %}

### 3. Authorize RM 150.00 (not captured yet)
POST http://localhost:8082/api/v1/payments
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Idempotency-Key: order-1001-attempt

{
  "amount": 15000,
  "currency": "MYR",
  "cardToken": "{{cardToken}}",
  "capture": false,
  "description": "Order #1001"
}

> {% client.global.set("paymentId", response.body.id); %}

### 4. Retry the exact same request: returns the SAME payment, header Idempotent-Replayed: true
POST http://localhost:8082/api/v1/payments
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Idempotency-Key: order-1001-attempt

{
  "amount": 15000,
  "currency": "MYR",
  "cardToken": "{{cardToken}}",
  "capture": false,
  "description": "Order #1001"
}

### 5. Partially capture RM 120.00 (remaining RM 30.00 hold is released)
POST http://localhost:8082/api/v1/payments/{{paymentId}}/capture
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

{ "amount": 12000 }

### 6. Refund RM 20.00
POST http://localhost:8082/api/v1/payments/{{paymentId}}/refunds
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

{ "amount": 2000 }

### 7. Try to refund more than is left: 422
POST http://localhost:8082/api/v1/payments/{{paymentId}}/refunds
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

{ "amount": 999999 }

### 8. Declined card (ends in 0002)
POST http://localhost:8083/api/v1/tokens
Content-Type: application/json

{ "pan": "4000000000000002", "expiryMonth": 12, "expiryYear": 2030 }

> {% client.global.set("declineToken", response.body.token); %}

###
POST http://localhost:8082/api/v1/payments
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Idempotency-Key: order-1002-attempt

{ "amount": 5000, "currency": "MYR", "cardToken": "{{declineToken}}", "capture": true }

### 9. Ledger in settlement-service (filled asynchronously via Kafka)
GET http://localhost:8084/api/v1/ledger?merchantId={{merchantId}}

### 10. Run settlement for today (normally runs nightly at 00:05 UTC for yesterday).
###     Replace the date with today's date (UTC).
POST http://localhost:8084/api/v1/settlements/run?date=2026-09-30

### 11. Running the same date again: 409 (Spring Batch job instance already complete)
POST http://localhost:8084/api/v1/settlements/run?date=2026-09-30

### 12. Settlement report
GET http://localhost:8084/api/v1/settlements?merchantId={{merchantId}}
